   242	    The command's cycle is proved to be one the resume replayed, from the result's receipt and the
   243	    resume's banner: its row (receipt tick T, plus one) lies after the checkpoint the resume began
   244	    from (tick M) and at or before the tick it recovered (N), so M <= T < N. A cadence checkpoint
   245	    that lands between the result and the kill would hold the command's cycle, and the replay would
   246	    then prove nothing about it: that setup is not counted, and the test sets up again."""
