   199	## Trying it without a credential
   200	
   201	The smoke stack brings up three agents and their recorders, answers them from a
   202	stub model that replies on cue instead of a real one, and mounts the contract
   203	fixture as the window, on scratch directories with a dummy key and its own
   204	compose project. It costs nothing. A second stack runs the same fleet with the
   205	vehicle as the window (`live/test_vehicle.py`); it replaces the first. One smoke
   206	stack at a time: a stack holds a lock every checkout of this user shares from
   207	its start to its `down`, and refuses to start while another smoke project is
   208	running. Every container the run starts is capped by the kernel -- each stack
   209	service (`CAPS` in `live/stack.py`: CPUs, and memory with no swap past it, read
   210	back from each container's cgroup before any test runs) and the containment
   211	check's image sweep -- and the live run refuses to start a stack outside a
   212	capped user scope, which holds pytest and the docker clients:
   213	
   214	```sh
   215	systemd-run --user --scope -p CPUQuota=35% -p MemoryMax=1G nice -n 19 python3 -m pytest live -q
   216	```
   217	
   218	Together that is 4.95 CPUs and 13.25 GiB of the live run's 5 CPUs and 14 GiB
   219	(Governance, 2026-10-11). Not capped: the docker daemon's own work, which the
   220	remainder is left for, and the image builds. The builds run one at a time;
   221	Docker's default builder runs their steps inside the daemon, and this harness
   222	sets no limit on them.
   223	
   224	It builds the image, runs the containment and acceptance checks against the
   225	running stack — no route out, the binds, the caps, a `done`, a reseed — and
   226	tears it down. It takes a few minutes, and it is the fastest way to see whether
   227	the world is intact after a change.
   228	
   229	## The vehicle
   230	
   231	The `vehicle` profile runs the spacecraft: one executive for every agent's
   232	window, with no network, its private state (checkpoints, its lock and the
   233	durable per-cycle record) on a `/state` image nothing else mounts. The windows
   234	it serves are `VEHICLE_SLUGS`, which compose fills from the roster; without a
   235	roster it serves one window called `vehicle`, for a probe in a stack with no
